   "captions": [
    {
     "start": 4.705,
     "end": 6.271,
     "lines": [
      "This is CardioLens."
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 6.455,
     "end": 11.734,
     "lines": [
      "Routine clinical data goes in, and a 3D",
      "heart shows where coronary risk is likely"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 11.784,
     "end": 14.1,
     "lines": [
      "to be, artery by artery."
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s01_problem",
   "title": "The problem",
   "chapter": 1,
   "kind": "card",
   "name": "problem",
   "start": 514,
   "duration": 911,
   "lead": 0.6,
   "tail": 0.8,
   "voice": 28.968,
   "audio": "voice/s01_problem.wav",
   "cues": {
    "goal": 10.797,
    "table": 25.653
   },
   "clips": [],
   "captions": [
    {
     "start": 0.705,
     "end": 4.797,
     "lines": [
      "Cardiovascular disease remains a leading",
      "cause of death worldwide,"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 4.942,
     "end": 9.218,
     "lines": [
      "and a narrowed coronary artery is usually",
      "confirmed by angiography,"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 9.271,
     "end": 10.613,
     "lines": [
      "an invasive test."
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 10.797,
     "end": 14.142,
     "lines": [
      "Track A asks a different question: can",
      "routine data,"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 14.192,
     "end": 18.8,
     "lines": [
      "such as age, blood pressure, an ECG and a",
      "few lab values,"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 18.85,
     "end": 23.021,
     "lines": [
      "predict coronary artery disease and the",
      "narrowing of each main artery,"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 23.1,
     "end": 25.442,
     "lines": [
      "and show it on an interactive 3D model?"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 25.653,
     "end": 29.416,
     "lines": [
      "Here is every requirement, and where",
      "CardioLens meets it."
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s02a_data",
   "title": "Dataset and leakage rule",
   "chapter": 2,
   "kind": "card",
   "name": "data",
   "start": 1470,
   "duration": 831,
   "lead": 0.4,
   "tail": 0.6,
   "voice": 26.712,
   "audio": "voice/s02a_data.wav",
   "cues": {
    "audit": 14.545,
    "leak": 18.518
   },
   "clips": [],
   "captions": [
    {
     "start": 0.518,
     "end": 4.847,
     "lines": [
      "We used the extension of the Z-Alizadeh",
      "Sani dataset from UCI:"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 4.939,
     "end": 10.229,
     "lines": [
      "303 patients, 55 features, and four",
      "targets: CAD,"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 10.361,
     "end": 14.361,
     "lines": [
      "plus the LAD, LCX and RCA arteries."
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 14.545,
     "end": 18.321,
     "lines": [
      "No values were missing, and a constant",
      "column was dropped."
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 18.518,
     "end": 21.255,
     "lines": [
      "The label columns are never model inputs."
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 21.439,
     "end": 25.584,
     "lines": [
      "That's asserted before every fit, and the",
      "API rejects them:"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 25.65,
     "end": 26.979,
     "lines": [
      "requirement 1d."
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s02b_validation",
   "title": "Features and validation",
   "chapter": 2,
   "kind": "card",
   "name": "validation",
   "start": 2302,
   "duration": 576,
   "lead": 0.3,
   "tail": 0.6,
   "voice": 18.312,
   "audio": "voice/s02b_validation.wav",
   "cues": {
    "holdout": 6.853,
    "cv": 10.511,
    "ci": 14.839
   },
   "clips": [],
   "captions": [
    {
     "start": 0.418,
     "end": 4.221,
     "lines": [
      "We add clinical features, such as a",
      "pretest probability,"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 4.287,
     "end": 6.668,
     "lines": [
      "kidney function and lipid ratios."
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 6.853,
     "end": 10.313,
     "lines": [
      "Twenty percent of patients are held out",
      "until the very end."
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 10.511,
     "end": 14.774,
     "lines": [
      "The rest go through five-by-five",
      "cross-validation with nested tuning,"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 14.839,
     "end": 18.471,
     "lines": [
      "and confidence intervals come from a",
      "thousand bootstrap resamples."
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s02c_models",
   "title": "Models, strategies, calibration",
   "chapter": 2,
   "kind": "card",
   "name": "models",
   "start": 2878,
   "duration": 697,
   "lead": 0.3,
   "tail": 0.6,
   "voice": 22.32,
   "audio": "voice/s02c_models.wav",
   "cues": {
    "strategy": 7.774,
    "calib": 15.037
   },
   "clips": [],
   "captions": [
    {
     "start": 0.405,
     "end": 3.603,
     "lines": [
      "Nine model families were compared for",
      "every target,"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 3.668,
     "end": 7.563,
     "lines": [
      "from logistic regression to boosting and",
      "stacked ensembles."
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 7.774,
     "end": 13.274,
     "lines": [
      "For the arteries, independent models did",
      "as well as chained or hierarchical ones,"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 13.405,
     "end": 14.853,
     "lines": [
      "so we kept the simplest."
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 15.037,
     "end": 19.326,
     "lines": [
      "Every model is calibrated, so eighty",
      "percent means about eight in ten,"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 19.432,
     "end": 22.471,
     "lines": [
      "with tuned thresholds and three risk",
      "tiers."
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s02d_results",
   "title": "Results and explanations",
   "chapter": 2,
   "kind": "card",
   "name": "results",
   "start": 3575,
   "duration": 860,
   "lead": 0.3,
   "tail": 0.8,
   "voice": 27.576,
   "audio": "voice/s02d_results.wav",
   "cues": {
    "shap": 19.195,
    "latency": 25.326
   },
   "clips": [],
   "captions": [
    {
     "start": 0.405,
     "end": 6.839,
     "lines": [
      "On the untouched hold-out set, the ROC-AUC",
      "is 0.895 for CAD,"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 6.932,
     "end": 17.276,
     "lines": [
      "0.832 for LAD, 0.768 for LCX and 0.741 for",
      "RCA, with confidence intervals and every"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 17.326,
     "end": 19.011,
     "lines": [
      "metric from requirement 1e."
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 19.195,
     "end": 23.066,
     "lines": [
      "Each estimate is explained with exact SHAP",
      "values,"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 23.116,
     "end": 27.721,
     "lines": [
      "mapped back to the raw measurements, in",
      "about 150 milliseconds."
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s03a_mapping",
   "title": "From probability to picture",
   "chapter": 3,
   "kind": "card",
   "name": "mapping",
   "start": 4480,
   "duration": 738,
   "lead": 0.4,
   "tail": 0.6,
   "voice": 23.592,
   "audio": "voice/s03a_mapping.wav",
   "cues": {
    "scale": 11.768,
    "flag": 17.321
   },
   "clips": [],
   "captions": [
    {
     "start": 0.505,
     "end": 2.782,
     "lines": [
      "How does a probability become a picture?"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 2.979,
     "end": 7.479,
     "lines": [
      "One anatomy map holds every mesh name,",
      "colour and label,"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 7.637,
     "end": 11.584,
     "lines": [
      "and a pure function turns each prediction",
      "into a render-ready scene."
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 11.768,
     "end": 16.284,
     "lines": [
      "Colour shows probability, on one shared",
      "scale that is safe for colour-blind"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 16.334,
     "end": 20.811,
     "lines": [
      "viewers. Crossing a threshold adds an",
      "outline and a pulse,"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 20.861,
     "end": 23.847,
     "lines": [
      "and every estimate carries a reliability",
      "badge."
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s03b_rules",
   "title": "No over-claiming",
   "chapter": 3,
   "kind": "card",
   "name": "rules",
   "start": 5218,
   "duration": 638,
   "lead": 0.3,
   "tail": 0.8,
   "voice": 20.16,
   "audio": "voice/s03b_rules.wav",
   "cues": {
    "overlays": 8.576,
    "whatif": 16.734
   },
   "clips": [],
   "captions": [
    {
     "start": 0.418,
     "end": 4.116,
     "lines": [
      "The data says whether an artery is",
      "narrowed, but not where."
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 4.313,
     "end": 8.379,
     "lines": [
      "So whole arteries are coloured, and",
      "unlabelled branches stay neutral."
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 8.576,
     "end": 13.447,
     "lines": [
      "Optional overlays show perfusion",
      "territories, and the body regions behind"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 13.497,
     "end": 16.55,
     "lines": [
      "each risk factor, never the disease",
      "itself."
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 16.734,
     "end": 20.313,
     "lines": [
      "And what-if shows associations, not",
      "treatment effects."
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s04a_source",
   "title": "The heart model",
   "chapter": 4,
   "kind": "card",
   "name": "heart_source",
   "start": 5901,
   "duration": 624,
   "lead": 0.4,
   "tail": 0.6,
   "voice": 19.8,
   "audio": "voice/s04a_source.wav",
   "cues": {
    "sketchfab": 6.466
   },
   "clips": [],
   "captions": [
    {
     "start": 0.505,
     "end": 1.5999999999999999,
     "lines": [
      "Building the heart."
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 1.65,
     "end": 6.216,
     "lines": [
      "Our first version was a procedural heart,",
      "which is still kept as a fallback."
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 6.466,
     "end": 11.479,
     "lines": [
      "For realism, we moved to the Realistic",
      "Human Heart by neshallads on Sketchfab,"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 11.637,
     "end": 13.979,
     "lines": [
      "under CC BY 4.0."
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 14.163,
     "end": 18.442,
     "lines": [
      "A headless Blender script aligns it,",
      "scales it to twelve centimetres,"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 18.492,
     "end": 20.045,
     "lines": [
      "and splits it into parts."
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s04b_build",
   "title": "Vessels and budgets",
   "chapter": 4,
   "kind": "card",
   "name": "heart_build",
   "start": 6525,
   "duration": 720,
   "lead": 0.3,
   "tail": 0.5,
   "voice": 23.208,
   "audio": "voice/s04b_build.wav",
   "cues": {
    "looks": 8.576,
    "lite": 15.866
   },
   "clips": [],
   "captions": [
    {
     "start": 0.405,
     "end": 5.026,
     "lines": [
      "Its coronaries were only painted on, so we",
      "traced them along the grooves,"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 5.076,
     "end": 8.379,
     "lines": [
      "smoothed them, and swept them into real",
      "tubes."
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 8.576,
     "end": 11.958,
     "lines": [
      "One file carries a realistic and a",
      "clinical look,"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 12.011,
     "end": 15.682,
     "lines": [
      "plus invisible picking shapes and outline",
      "shells."
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 15.866,
     "end": 20.697,
     "lines": [
      "It's compressed to about 1.6 megabytes,",
      "with a lighter version for phones,"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 20.747,
     "end": 23.379,
     "lines": [
      "and a validator checks every name and",
      "budget."
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
